# Auth-Regeln

## Rollen (RBAC)

Hierarchie in `src/lib/rbac.ts`: `VIEWER < MEMBER < TEAM < ADMIN < OWNER`

- **Kunden:** `VIEWER` (read-only) / `MEMBER` (read+write) – Spalte `customers.portal_role`
- **Staff:** `TEAM` / `ADMIN` / `OWNER` – Tabelle `staff_users`; ENV-Admin → `OWNER` via `ensureEnvOwnerStaff`
- **Middleware:** Staff → `/admin/*`, Kunden → `/customer/*`
- **API:** `requireRole`, `requireAdminAuth` (≥ADMIN), `requireCustomerAuth` (≥VIEWER), `requireMemberAuth` (≥MEMBER)

## Token

- Erstellung: `createToken` in `src/lib/auth.ts` (`jsonwebtoken`)
- Edge-Verify: `jwtVerify` (`jose`) in Middleware
- Env: `JWT_SECRET` muss gesetzt sein

## Admin-Login

- TAN-Flow: `admin-request-tan` → `admin-verify-tan` → Session-Cookie

## Kundenportal

- Anlage bei Funnel-4 `intent: contact` (`getOrCreateCustomerWithNumber`)
- Aktivierung: `/customer/activate?token=…`, Portal-Links per E-Mail (`portal-activation`)

## Sicherheit

- Keine Secrets loggen oder committen
- API-Routen: `requireAdminAuth` für Admin-Endpunkte
- Passwort-Hashing: `bcryptjs`
